WEBVTT

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.084
Yes, 10!

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:38.019
Well done, Cubonius.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.893
You decapitated the unicorn.

00:01:39.998 --> 00:01:41.329
- Swell.
- All right.

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:44.266
Oh, oh!
We search his tail pouch for treasure.

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:47.600
Deep in the unicorn's rump sack, you find

00:01:50.075 --> 00:01:51.542
60 gold pieces

00:01:51.643 --> 00:01:56.273
and a mysterious scrap of cloth bearing
the unmistakable stench of dwarf urine.

00:01:56.381 --> 00:01:59.316
The same stench
that was on the bed linens at the inn?

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:02.114
- The very same.
- Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:04.985
I cast a spell of detect magic.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:09.222
What you doing, mini-meatbags?
Underage gambling?

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:10.386
Shame on you.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:11.622
Count me in.

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:14.595
We're not gambling.
We're playing Dungeons &amp; Dragons.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.727
Right now, we're fighting for our lives
in the lair of the dragon queen.

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:22.434
Wrong, right now you're
ass-deep in a folding chair.

00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:26.910
Yes, but in my imagination
I'm riding a golden Pegasus.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:28.274
Giddy up, Sparky!

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.406
Am I the only one seeing him sitting here
with peanut butter on his face?

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:34.452
Bender, were you built
without an imagination?

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:37.647
What? Don't be stupid, of course not.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:40.488
It just hasn't descended yet.

00:02:45.397 --> 00:02:48.127
Fry, do I have an imagination?

00:02:48.233 --> 00:02:50.360
I don't know, Bender. Why do you ask?

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:52.403
Were the other boys making fun of you?

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:55.768
Mmm-hmm.
They said I couldn't imagine things.

00:02:55.874 --> 00:02:58.707
Well, you never know unless you try.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.971
Like, I didn't know
if I could swallow a softball,

00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:03.741
so I gave it my best shot and voilа!

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:05.716
Wait, that's not it.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:07.377
There she blows.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.084
Warning, out of dark matter fuel.

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:12.485
That's not a warning.

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:15.754
A warning is supposed to come
before something bad happens.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:19.524
Warning,
engines will shut down in one second.

00:03:19.631 --> 00:03:21.098
That's more like it.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:27.761
Uh-oh.

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:30.467
This space neighborhood
looks kind of sketchy.

00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:35.173
Rock 'n' roll.

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:38.775
That punk stole our hood ornament.

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:41.648
Now no one will know
we have the LX package.

00:03:41.753 --> 00:03:44.221
We need dark matter and we need it fast.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:47.451
Fry, check Nibbler's litter box.
Maybe he dropped a steamer.

00:03:47.559 --> 00:03:48.617
Aye, aye, Captain.

00:03:52.464 --> 00:03:55.297
Yes! I've never been so excited
to see poop.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:56.726
Well, maybe once.

00:04:03.775 --> 00:04:05.367
There's gas in our ass.

00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:21.219
Can you believe the price of dark matter?

00:04:21.326 --> 00:04:25.023
It'd be cheaper to fill the tank
with Nobel Prize winners' sperm.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:30.067
Total dark matter purchased, $632. 14.

00:04:30.168 --> 00:04:32.500
Your Speedpass will now be charged.

00:04:34.339 --> 00:04:35.670
You lousy...

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:38.174
Hey, gets a loads of that ugly ship.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:40.404
What shades of green is that? Puke?

00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:46.273
For your information
it's called Electric Mucus.

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:47.647
More like puke.

00:04:48.153 --> 00:04:49.552
Whoa!

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:53.716
Yeah, why don't you come a little closer
so my boot can hear you?

00:04:53.825 --> 00:04:57.226
Calm down, Leela.
You can vent tonight on your blog.

00:04:57.329 --> 00:05:00.730
What's the matters,
you couldn't affords the LX package?

00:05:00.899 --> 00:05:02.196
Puke-a-doodle-do.

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:04.525
You're making fun of our ship?

00:05:04.636 --> 00:05:07.104
Your ship is the most beat-up thing
I've ever seen,

00:05:07.205 --> 00:05:09.400
and I've seen Mickey Rourke's head.

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:11.601
Yeah, she's a little worky,

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:15.806
but you got to gets big time ugly to be
five-time winners at a demolition derby.

00:05:19.017 --> 00:05:22.043
That's five more times than we've won
or even entered.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:23.678
We do suck.

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:27.190
Yup, and it's gonna be six winses
after tonights.

00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:29.584
We'll sees abouts that.

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:35.633
Dark matter costs have tripled,
so we must reduce expenses.

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:38.965
Therefore, we will no longer provide
complimentary porno magazines

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:40.060
in the lounge.

00:05:41.873 --> 00:05:44.740
- Darn it.
- And no more wasting fuel.

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:48.540
From now on I'll be keeping a tight hold
on the keys to the ship,

00:05:48.647 --> 00:05:52.879
swallowing them before I go to bed
and recovering them the next morning.

00:05:54.519 --> 00:05:56.248
Professor, it's 4:00.

00:05:56.688 --> 00:05:59.486
4:00 in the evening? Then, good night.

00:06:03.528 --> 00:06:05.496
I don't care what the Professor says.

00:06:05.597 --> 00:06:09.931
We're entering that demolition derby
to prove our ship isn't a piece of junk.

00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:12.629
But won't that turn our ship
into a piece of junk?

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:14.672
Shut up, Zoidberg.

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:15.831
He's right, Leela.

00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:19.308
But we have no choice.
Rednecks insulted us.

00:06:19.411 --> 00:06:22.539
So? Let it go.
Don't let your temper get the better of...

00:06:22.647 --> 00:06:24.842
Rednecks!

00:06:31.723 --> 00:06:33.315
Using this magneto,

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:37.885
I will now guide the keys up the thorax
and out via the frontal face hole.

00:06:40.165 --> 00:06:46.832
That's the storage locker, the bolt,
the other bolt, pay dirt!

00:06:48.907 --> 00:06:53.310
Rocket ship

00:06:56.815 --> 00:07:01.445
Rocket ship

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.555
Greetings, sports fans.

00:07:10.662 --> 00:07:13.187
Though whether
this outpouring of inbreds

00:07:13.298 --> 00:07:15.960
can in fact be classified as a sport

00:07:16.067 --> 00:07:20.197
is a subject of no small scholarly debate.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:25.206
Well, wells, well, if it ain'ts
Princess Pukerella

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.471
and her pukey puke-mobile.

00:07:27.579 --> 00:07:30.070
Oh, yeah? Well... Shut up.

00:07:30.182 --> 00:07:31.979
- Good comeback, Leela.
- You shut up, too.

00:07:33.385 --> 00:07:36.354
Rich Little, here, as Howard Cosell.

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:41.051
And now to grace us with its rendition
of the national anthem,

00:07:41.159 --> 00:07:44.595
please welcome what is left
of the Dixie Chicks

00:07:44.696 --> 00:07:48.462
after their tragic
matter transporter accident.

00:07:49.267 --> 00:07:51.565
We're in horrible pain.

00:07:53.338 --> 00:07:55.465
And we are underway.

00:08:10.121 --> 00:08:11.588
Whoas!

00:08:11.756 --> 00:08:13.587
Yes! Now we're inflicting.

00:08:13.692 --> 00:08:18.629
Outstanding! Tonight we are
witnessing a veritable clinic

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:23.793
and that ludicrous hullabaloo
known as demolition derby.

00:08:33.845 --> 00:08:36.143
Way to kill the franchise, Bakula.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:42.482
Ladies and gentlemen,
we are down to our final two ships.

00:08:42.587 --> 00:08:48.287
In the storied annals of demolition derby,
today will surely be remembered,

00:08:48.393 --> 00:08:51.692
if only as the day
upon which I was absorbed

00:08:51.796 --> 00:08:56.563
into that hideous conglomeration
once known as the Dixie Chicks.

00:08:57.936 --> 00:08:59.733
Buckle your sphincters.

00:09:02.941 --> 00:09:05.273
- No! No!
- No!

00:09:05.377 --> 00:09:09.211
- That broad's insanes.
- But you're insansier, right?

00:09:09.748 --> 00:09:11.579
Nah, I guess nots.

00:09:11.683 --> 00:09:14.743
I've decideds to relax
and enjoy life from now ons.

00:09:28.033 --> 00:09:30.228
Yes! We did it!

00:09:31.903 --> 00:09:34.895
And Planet Express takes the trophy.

00:09:39.578 --> 00:09:43.105
Rocket ship

00:09:53.825 --> 00:09:56.623
Now, I'll use the magnet
to get the keys back in there.

00:09:56.728 --> 00:09:59.754
What? You mean I cut a big hole
in him for nothing?

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:06.468
Don't worry, the Professor
won't even remember

00:10:06.571 --> 00:10:07.765
that he has a spaceship.

00:10:09.007 --> 00:10:10.406
My precious spaceship.

00:10:10.508 --> 00:10:14.342
My lone source of joy
in the cold December of my days.

00:10:14.446 --> 00:10:19.008
Come, friends. Let's take her for a spin
to the malt shop like old times.

00:10:19.117 --> 00:10:22.951
Leela to Zoidberg.
Execute Distraction Protocol Alpha.

00:10:23.054 --> 00:10:24.146
Roger that.

00:10:24.823 --> 00:10:27.291
Look at me! Look at me! Look at me!

00:10:28.627 --> 00:10:29.958
Don't look at me.

00:10:34.699 --> 00:10:37.463
Yes, she's a wonderful ship, all right.

00:10:37.569 --> 00:10:41.699
As beautiful now
as the day I got botched laser eye surgery.

00:10:42.273 --> 00:10:43.433
Now, that's odd.

00:10:43.541 --> 00:10:45.372
What's the fuel gauge doing on the...

00:10:47.145 --> 00:10:49.170
Great Godzilla's gonads!

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:52.772
Who wasted precious fuel?
Answer now or be punished.

00:10:53.084 --> 00:10:57.077
- All right, fine. I admit it.
- You will be punished.

00:10:58.923 --> 00:11:00.447
Oh, my gosh, 20!

00:11:00.558 --> 00:11:02.048
Yeah.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.025
Your pole arm does double damage,

00:11:04.129 --> 00:11:07.121
and the gelatinous cube dies
in horrible poverty.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:10.624
- All right.
- Hooray.

00:11:10.735 --> 00:11:14.193
I proceed to cast a spell of darkness.

00:11:14.873 --> 00:11:16.204
Most ingenious.

00:11:18.176 --> 00:11:19.768
- Bender?
- Me?

00:11:19.878 --> 00:11:23.473
I cast a spell of darkness.

00:11:25.283 --> 00:11:26.614
Pretty imaginative, huh?

00:11:26.718 --> 00:11:30.916
No, you just did the same thing as me,
but with a dumb noise.

00:11:31.122 --> 00:11:32.089
Oh...

00:11:32.857 --> 00:11:37.590
You're right. I'm great in every way
except I have no imagination.

00:11:37.696 --> 00:11:42.258
All I ever wanted is to play
this magical game and I can't.

00:11:42.367 --> 00:11:45.825
Yes, you can. You just have
to lose yourself in the fantasy.

00:11:45.937 --> 00:11:49.100
You have to believe the impossible
is merely preposterous.

00:11:49.207 --> 00:11:51.300
Okay. Here goes.

00:11:51.876 --> 00:11:52.934
Visor down.

00:11:53.645 --> 00:11:55.704
I believe, I believe.

00:11:57.082 --> 00:11:58.413
Ooh.

00:11:59.084 --> 00:12:01.314
I did it! I imagined something.

00:12:01.419 --> 00:12:05.822
For 1.3 milliseconds,
I truly believed I was a noble robot

00:12:05.924 --> 00:12:07.414
in days of yonder.

00:12:07.892 --> 00:12:09.359
Way to go, Bender.

00:12:09.461 --> 00:12:11.827
What is thy character's name, good sir?

00:12:11.996 --> 00:12:13.463
Uh, um...

00:12:13.698 --> 00:12:16.326
I am Titanius Inglesmith,

00:12:16.434 --> 00:12:18.334
fancy man of Cornwood.

00:12:20.839 --> 00:12:24.639
Everybody out of the conference room.
I am calling a conference.

00:12:24.743 --> 00:12:26.301
Everybody get in here.

00:12:26.845 --> 00:12:31.509
You wasted precious fuel just because
you were insulted by some redneck yokel

00:12:31.616 --> 00:12:33.174
from beyond the stars?

00:12:33.284 --> 00:12:36.014
- It was only half a ball.
- That's not the point.

00:12:36.154 --> 00:12:37.883
Your temper is out of control.

00:12:37.989 --> 00:12:39.957
And to think I'd have never even known

00:12:40.058 --> 00:12:44.324
if it weren't for the lengthy
and unsolicited tattling of Dr. Zoidberg.

00:12:44.696 --> 00:12:47.130
She also took home
two rolls of Scotch tape.

00:12:47.232 --> 00:12:49.132
Thank you, Dr. Zoidberg.

00:12:49.234 --> 00:12:51.930
Hermes, incentivize that employee.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:59.042
As for you, Leela, I'm letting you off
with a warning.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:00.973
Oh, thank you.

00:13:01.079 --> 00:13:05.709
A warning that will be administered
by this 50,000-volt shock collar.

00:13:06.951 --> 00:13:10.114
Zoidberg, I'm gonna put my boot
so far up your cloaca, you'll be...

00:13:10.221 --> 00:13:11.347
Ow!

00:13:11.456 --> 00:13:15.722
The collar will be triggered any time
your thoughts turn to violence.

00:13:16.394 --> 00:13:17.952
Profanity.

00:13:18.062 --> 00:13:19.324
Son of a...

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:21.955
Or perversions of a sexual nature.

00:13:23.001 --> 00:13:23.968
Ow!

00:13:24.769 --> 00:13:27.932
Sorry, it's the only collar
they had in stock at Office Depot.

00:13:28.039 --> 00:13:31.406
I hope you picked up some Scotch tape
while you were there.

00:13:33.578 --> 00:13:34.602
That's a good one.

00:13:41.886 --> 00:13:45.378
Imagine, if you will,
an announcer you can barely understand.

00:13:45.657 --> 00:13:46.646
He refers to a...

00:13:47.826 --> 00:13:49.225
But you're not quite sure what he said.

00:13:49.427 --> 00:13:52.954
He seems to be eating something,
or perhaps he's a little drunk.

00:13:53.064 --> 00:13:57.433
It's remotely possible that he just said
something about The Scary Door.

00:14:12.684 --> 00:14:13.946
Firing, sir!

00:14:14.285 --> 00:14:16.344
It's all over. Our guns and bombs

00:14:16.454 --> 00:14:20.447
- are useless against the aliens.
- The saucers! Theys are crashing!

00:14:25.463 --> 00:14:28.990
In the end, it was not guns
or bombs that defeated the aliens,

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:32.831
but that humblest of all God's creatures,
the Tyrannosaurus Rex.

00:14:38.743 --> 00:14:42.110
I can't believe TiVo suggested
that piece of... Ow!

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.742
Come on, Hermes.

00:14:43.848 --> 00:14:46.942
Surely you have the authority
to remove this damn collar.

00:14:47.118 --> 00:14:50.713
Alas, no.
I got the key but not the authority.

00:14:50.855 --> 00:14:51.822
Yeow!

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:54.620
Well, who does have the authority?

00:14:54.726 --> 00:14:57.388
Only the staff doctor.
You'll have to convince him

00:14:57.495 --> 00:14:59.224
that you have resolved your anger issues.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:03.198
I don't have any god...
mother... anger issues.

00:15:04.202 --> 00:15:08.798
As your dwarf-skin canoe rounds a bend
you suddenly see...

00:15:08.907 --> 00:15:11.034
A terrifying red dragon.

00:15:12.377 --> 00:15:14.072
What do we do? What do we do?

00:15:14.178 --> 00:15:15.509
Wait, I know.

00:15:15.613 --> 00:15:18.241
I make use of my round of fireballs.

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:25.346
Everyone knows red dragons
are immune to fireballs

00:15:25.456 --> 00:15:28.152
as well as all other forms
of incendiary attack.

00:15:28.259 --> 00:15:32.593
Yes, but I aim not at the dragon
but at the river itself,

00:15:32.697 --> 00:15:35.757
to create a shroud of steam
through which we can escape.

00:15:35.867 --> 00:15:37.459
Whoa!

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:41.595
Sweet pony of Sierra Leone, it worked!

00:15:42.573 --> 00:15:44.040
- We did it!
- Yeah!

00:15:45.176 --> 00:15:46.575
Bender, smell this milk.

00:15:46.678 --> 00:15:49.909
I go not by the name of Bender,
you fleshy fool,

00:15:50.014 --> 00:15:54.542
I am Titanius Inglesmith,
fancy man of Cornwood.

00:15:57.822 --> 00:15:59.813
Professor, something's bothering me.

00:15:59.924 --> 00:16:03.325
Well, you can
always talk to me about anything, Fry.

00:16:03.428 --> 00:16:05.055
What's on your mind?

00:16:05.163 --> 00:16:07.495
Well, it's about my friend Bender.

00:16:07.632 --> 00:16:09.463
Mmm. I see.

00:16:09.767 --> 00:16:14.170
Show me on this anatomically correct doll
exactly where he touched you.

00:16:14.272 --> 00:16:18.709
No, it's nothing like that.
It's just that I am worried about him.

00:16:18.843 --> 00:16:21.710
He's being playing an awful lot
of Dungeons &amp; Dragons.

00:16:21.813 --> 00:16:26.079
Dungeons &amp;... Good God!
Hasn't he seen the Afterschool Special?

00:16:26.818 --> 00:16:28.308
You've got to talk to him, Fry.

00:16:28.419 --> 00:16:32.082
Make him quit now,
before he completely loses his mind.

00:16:32.457 --> 00:16:34.982
- Okay, I will.
- Good boy.

00:16:35.259 --> 00:16:37.853
Just don't let him touch you down there.

00:16:41.132 --> 00:16:45.535
Well, here's your problem, right here.
You've got a skull embedded in your head.

00:16:45.837 --> 00:16:50.137
You're absolutely right, Doctor.
Can the collar come off now?

00:16:50.675 --> 00:16:54.634
Let me just peel your head a little
and see if I can get that skull out.

00:16:58.349 --> 00:17:02.513
So, you tell me, little miss expert,
why always with the temper?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.451
Calm down for once and think.

00:17:04.555 --> 00:17:07.854
Here, enjoy a relaxing spritz
from my empathy bladder.

00:17:09.594 --> 00:17:12.620
What is it, already?
What's the cause of your anger?

00:17:12.964 --> 00:17:16.127
I guess I would have to say, I hate you.

00:17:16.801 --> 00:17:20.999
I'm beginning to understand.
It all goes back to your parents.

00:17:21.105 --> 00:17:23.300
- What?
- You have a resentment

00:17:23.408 --> 00:17:25.808
because they pushed you
to study medicine,

00:17:25.943 --> 00:17:29.572
when all you ever wanted
was to be a song-and-dance man.

00:17:34.385 --> 00:17:37.286
Why? Why?

00:17:37.455 --> 00:17:39.320
I was raised in an orphanarium.

00:17:39.424 --> 00:17:40.721
My parents are sewer mutants

00:17:40.825 --> 00:17:43.259
who I never even met
until a few years ago.

00:17:43.394 --> 00:17:46.955
Then you've got to go to them
and work this song-and-dance stuff out.

00:17:47.065 --> 00:17:50.694
Maybe have them cook me nice dinner.
No scallions. I hate them.

00:17:51.402 --> 00:17:54.963
- Amy, cancel my appointments.
- Stop calling me.

00:18:01.979 --> 00:18:04.209
Bender, please don't get mad,

00:18:04.315 --> 00:18:07.773
but I think you might be playing too much
Dungeons &amp; Dragons.

00:18:07.919 --> 00:18:09.910
You're absolutely right, Fry.

00:18:10.021 --> 00:18:13.513
I almost went insane,
but after this heart-to-heart talk,

00:18:13.624 --> 00:18:15.683
- I've decided to quit.
- Really?

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:17.953
Whew! That's a load off my toad.

00:18:18.062 --> 00:18:19.825
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:18:19.931 --> 00:18:22.627
I'm off to slay the werewolf
of Goblin Mountain.

00:18:30.908 --> 00:18:32.739
On guard, man-wench!

00:18:32.844 --> 00:18:34.812
Prepare to cross blades.

00:18:35.146 --> 00:18:37.046
You couldn't afford it, honey.

00:18:40.418 --> 00:18:45.412
Foolish leprechaun, I scoop your treasure
in the name of the fancy men.

00:18:46.891 --> 00:18:50.019
He also left a small pile
of treasure on the living room rug.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:54.621
Foul dragon, meet thy doom.

00:19:14.118 --> 00:19:16.814
- Would you like a napkin, Doctor?
- Thank you.

00:19:18.556 --> 00:19:22.492
Satisfied, Zoidberg?
My relationship with my parents is fine.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:26.423
Now, hold on, Leela.
Maybe this torture collar is good for you.

00:19:26.531 --> 00:19:27.498
What? Ow!

00:19:27.632 --> 00:19:29.122
It'll control your temper.

00:19:29.233 --> 00:19:32.566
Men like a woman who's not always
slamming their head in the car door.

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:35.138
She's right. That's what first attracted me
to your mother.

00:19:37.341 --> 00:19:40.742
So, Leela, I understand your friend here
is a physician,

00:19:40.845 --> 00:19:43.075
and I'm not seeing a ring on his claw.

00:19:43.181 --> 00:19:45.240
Mom, he's a cockroach from outer space.

00:19:46.551 --> 00:19:48.985
Good, Leela, work that anger out.

00:19:49.086 --> 00:19:51.816
Excuse me a moment,
I'm swarming with parasites.

00:19:56.127 --> 00:19:58.618
Hey, it's what's-his-name from the surface.

00:19:58.763 --> 00:20:00.162
The bi-clops.

00:20:00.932 --> 00:20:04.698
Have you seen Bender? He's gone nuts.
Also, smell this milk.

00:20:08.172 --> 00:20:10.663
Prepare for a surprise attack.

00:20:11.909 --> 00:20:13.206
Someone do something.

00:20:13.311 --> 00:20:16.747
I would, but... Ow! Take my collar off.

00:20:16.847 --> 00:20:18.838
I can't, I'm still eating.

00:20:22.353 --> 00:20:23.684
Help me, Leela.

00:20:26.657 --> 00:20:29.956
I cast upon thee a spell of fireball!

00:20:44.041 --> 00:20:45.372
No.

00:20:45.476 --> 00:20:47.103
Not the spork.

00:20:47.445 --> 00:20:51.779
Beholdeth, Titanius,
I cast a freeze ray upon you.

00:20:51.882 --> 00:20:56.080
That's ridiculous.
There's no such thing as a freeze ray.

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.182
- What, you mean a cone of coldness?
- Yeah, that.

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:04.618
No! No! Fancy men are defenseless
against cone of coldness.

00:21:06.297 --> 00:21:07.787
I'm freezing... What?

00:21:09.033 --> 00:21:10.796
Bender, no.

00:21:11.235 --> 00:21:14.204
When will young people learn that
Dungeons &amp; Dragons

00:21:14.305 --> 00:21:15.829
won't make you cool?

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:18.204
Relax, Fry. I'm a doctor.

00:21:18.309 --> 00:21:21.403
I'm sure the robot
will be just fine with a little help.

00:21:22.313 --> 00:21:24.543
Help, help.

00:21:25.349 --> 00:21:27.544
Help!

00:21:39.897 --> 00:21:41.728
Please, send in the patient.

00:21:41.899 --> 00:21:42.888
Yes, Doctor.

00:21:46.537 --> 00:21:52.806
So, Bender, I understand you're having
trouble separating fantasy from reality.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:55.003
Says who? Was it the bugbear?

00:21:55.112 --> 00:21:58.081
- Is he talking about me again?
- I understand.

00:21:58.182 --> 00:21:59.547
Commence therapy.

00:22:02.853 --> 00:22:04.878
Tell me about your feelings.

00:22:08.125 --> 00:22:09.422
Poor Bender.

00:22:09.527 --> 00:22:12.018
Says here to tell his friends he's at a spa.

00:22:12.396 --> 00:22:14.660
- So what happened to Bender?
- He's at a spa.

00:22:14.765 --> 00:22:17.233
Wow, there's a spa in the nut house?

00:22:17.335 --> 00:22:21.499
Friends, friends, stop everything.
There's food in this shaker.

00:22:25.443 --> 00:22:26.432
Ow!

00:22:26.544 --> 00:22:29.945
Enough already!
Can you please remove this anger collar?

00:22:30.047 --> 00:22:32.743
- Are you still angry?
- No. Ow!

00:22:32.883 --> 00:22:34.407
It also shocks you when you lie.

00:22:34.518 --> 00:22:36.884
Quiet, everyone. The network news is on.

00:22:36.987 --> 00:22:41.686
And if I, a 165-year-old man,
don't watch it, who will?

00:22:41.959 --> 00:22:45.326
Thankfully, the amazing talking horse
was rescued

00:22:45.429 --> 00:22:47.897
and safely returned
to the meat department.

00:22:50.801 --> 00:22:53.361
Turning to the less stupid portion
of our broadcast,

00:22:53.471 --> 00:22:58.101
fuel prices hit an all-time high today
due to the ongoing dark matter shortage.

00:22:58.209 --> 00:23:01.542
Earlier, our own Morbo
sat down with Mom,

00:23:01.645 --> 00:23:05.547
CEO of Mom 's Friendly
Multinational Energy Conglomerate.

00:23:15.493 --> 00:23:18.360
Oh! Hello, Morbo the Annihilator, here,

00:23:18.529 --> 00:23:22.431
sitting down to a delightful tea
in this fake living room set.

00:23:22.833 --> 00:23:24.528
Thank you for joining us, Mom.

00:23:24.635 --> 00:23:26.762
My pleasure, sugarplum.

00:23:26.971 --> 00:23:30.304
Mom, you control the world's
only dark matter mine.

00:23:30.741 --> 00:23:33.335
Tell us, why are fuel prices so high?

00:23:33.444 --> 00:23:35.309
Oh! It's terrible, isn't it?

00:23:35.746 --> 00:23:38.613
Dark matter is just so rare nowadays,

00:23:38.716 --> 00:23:42.482
but we'll keep pinching loaf after loaf
from the bowels of the earth,

00:23:42.586 --> 00:23:45.248
even if I lose money on every log.

00:23:45.423 --> 00:23:50.588
If you are losing money, how did you
post record profits last quarter?

00:23:52.196 --> 00:23:56.496
You look thin, care for one of my
famous pecan clusters?

00:23:58.135 --> 00:24:02.037
Morbo shouldn't. It will go straight
to Morbo's gargantuan forehead.

00:24:02.640 --> 00:24:06.337
Oh, what the heck? I guess I could destroy
one or two of them.

00:24:08.612 --> 00:24:11.672
Do people care enough to drill
for dark matter

00:24:11.782 --> 00:24:14.717
even in an Alaskan wildlife refuge?

00:24:15.252 --> 00:24:16.378
People do.

00:24:16.487 --> 00:24:21.015
Greedy old hag, taste the wrath
of my fuzzy slipper.

00:24:23.461 --> 00:24:27.522
Professor, why are you so hot and dusty
over this dark matter shortage?

00:24:28.966 --> 00:24:34.700
I bet you'd like to know.
I bet you'd like to know, indeed.

00:25:05.035 --> 00:25:07.401
Hello, Mother. How did the interview go?

00:25:07.505 --> 00:25:10.372
It made me want to puke my face off.

00:25:10.574 --> 00:25:12.667
- Where's my Thigh Blaster?
- Right here, Mom.

00:25:12.776 --> 00:25:14.744
- Shut up!
- Okay, thank you.

00:25:15.746 --> 00:25:17.873
Burn, you damn thighs. Burn!

00:25:18.415 --> 00:25:21.873
Mommy, are you upset
'cause of the dark matter shortage?

00:25:21.986 --> 00:25:24.648
There is no shortage,
you moronic ass-brain!

00:25:24.755 --> 00:25:26.154
There's not? But you said...

00:25:27.424 --> 00:25:32.691
Allow me to explain. Suppose this hand
represents current reserves of dark matter

00:25:32.796 --> 00:25:35.390
and this hand represents
consumer demand.

00:25:35.799 --> 00:25:37.096
Uh-huh.

00:25:42.806 --> 00:25:45.707
I just bet you'd like to know
why I'm so angry

00:25:45.809 --> 00:25:47.674
about this dark matter shortage.

00:25:47.778 --> 00:25:50.303
I bet very much you'd like to know.

00:25:50.414 --> 00:25:52.507
You're right, Professor.
We would like to know.

00:25:52.616 --> 00:25:55.813
Really? I didn't think anyone
was interested.

00:25:56.487 --> 00:25:59.979
It all started 30-odd years ago.

00:26:00.925 --> 00:26:04.361
I was working in Mom 's laboratories
for the third time

00:26:04.461 --> 00:26:07.589
after twice before realizing
how evil she was

00:26:07.765 --> 00:26:10.165
and vowing never to work for her again.

00:26:11.702 --> 00:26:16.435
But somehow the rich,
wrong stench of her boney charms

00:26:16.540 --> 00:26:18.508
kept calling me back.

00:26:20.110 --> 00:26:23.136
Don't stop, Professor. I'm getting aroused.

00:26:23.247 --> 00:26:27.877
Back in those days, dark matter
was just a worthless inert curiosity,

00:26:28.252 --> 00:26:30.982
and I was smashing it
in a particle accelerator,

00:26:31.088 --> 00:26:36.185
in an ill-conceived attempt
to create a more durable harpsichord wax.

00:26:36.927 --> 00:26:40.829
But, as Deepak Chopra taught us,
quantum physics means

00:26:40.931 --> 00:26:44.230
anything can happen at any time
for no reason.

00:26:44.368 --> 00:26:46.336
Also, eat plenty of oatmeal,

00:26:46.437 --> 00:26:48.598
and animals never had a war.

00:26:48.706 --> 00:26:50.537
Who's the real animals?

00:26:51.809 --> 00:26:57.441
And thus against all probabilities,
it happened.

00:27:06.423 --> 00:27:07.390
Dang!

00:27:07.524 --> 00:27:11.654
I'm sure I don't need to explain
that all dark matter in the universe

00:27:11.762 --> 00:27:15.721
is linked in the form
of a single non-local meta-particle.

00:27:17.034 --> 00:27:18.501
Stop patronizing us.

00:27:18.602 --> 00:27:23.198
So, in one instant, I had transformed
all dark matter everywhere

00:27:23.307 --> 00:27:25.605
into a new crystalline form...

00:27:25.943 --> 00:27:29.709
...making it the most potent fuel
since primitive man first ignited

00:27:29.813 --> 00:27:32.441
mastodon flatulence to heat his cave.

00:27:32.549 --> 00:27:36.451
I'm intrigued, Hubert.
You have my undivided attention.

00:27:45.029 --> 00:27:47.793
Shut up, you milk-sucking leeches!

00:27:48.832 --> 00:27:50.527
A new super fuel, eh?

00:27:50.668 --> 00:27:52.636
- We're rich.
- Indeed, we are.

00:27:52.836 --> 00:27:55.236
Not you, we. Us, we.

00:27:56.340 --> 00:27:58.774
I'm getting back together
with my ex-husband.

00:27:58.876 --> 00:28:00.366
Wernstrom!

00:28:03.213 --> 00:28:05.443
You've been played, Farnsworth.

00:28:05.549 --> 00:28:07.517
Played like a cheap harpsichord.

00:28:07.618 --> 00:28:10.382
Walt, fire that employee
like Mommy taught you.

00:28:18.762 --> 00:28:21.287
Professor, maybe I can help you
get even with Mom.

00:28:21.398 --> 00:28:25.061
I spend most of my time thinking about
how to get revenge on a bad boss.

00:28:25.169 --> 00:28:26.500
- Me, too.
- Likewise.

00:28:26.603 --> 00:28:28.366
I made a blinding powder.

00:28:28.472 --> 00:28:30.838
Thanks, but that won't be necessary

00:28:30.941 --> 00:28:33.341
because I have the ultimate weapon.

00:28:34.378 --> 00:28:38.212
You see, in the instant
the energy crystal was created,

00:28:38.315 --> 00:28:40.715
there also came into being
an opposite crystal

00:28:40.818 --> 00:28:43.252
made of pure anti-backwards energy.

00:28:44.221 --> 00:28:45.745
- Wow!
- Wow!

00:28:45.856 --> 00:28:47.790
- So?
- So, this!

00:28:47.891 --> 00:28:49.722
If ever the two crystals should meet,

00:28:49.827 --> 00:28:53.558
their wave functions would collapse
like Raymond Burr's trampoline,

00:28:53.664 --> 00:28:58.101
once again rendering all dark matter
inert and useless as fuel.

00:28:58.202 --> 00:28:59.567
But then we'll have no fuel.

00:28:59.670 --> 00:29:04.004
But once we free society
from dependence on Mom's dark matter,

00:29:04.108 --> 00:29:08.670
scientists will finally care enough
to develop cleaner, alternative fuels.

00:29:08.779 --> 00:29:10.406
Scientists like you?

00:29:10.514 --> 00:29:14.883
No, not me.
I'm too busy developing makeup for dogs.

00:29:14.985 --> 00:29:16.680
That's where the money is.

00:29:17.921 --> 00:29:20.617
This is our chance to teach Mom a lesson.
Come on!

00:29:20.724 --> 00:29:24.091
Let's take the anti-crystal
and shove it up Mom's regular crystal.

00:29:24.194 --> 00:29:25.786
- Yeah.
- Fight the power!

00:29:26.530 --> 00:29:30.227
There's just one, small problem,
and it's a big one.

00:29:30.334 --> 00:29:33.132
I hid the crystal
and I can't remember where.

00:29:33.270 --> 00:29:36.535
Well, surely it's just a matter of waiting
till you next move your bowels

00:29:36.640 --> 00:29:40.303
- and then using a potato masher...
- Don't you think I already tried that?

00:29:40.410 --> 00:29:44.073
No. I'm afraid, the crystal is lost forever.

00:29:46.450 --> 00:29:49.078
Nine? You did it.
You outwitted the fungus.

00:29:50.053 --> 00:29:51.315
Who needs girls?

00:29:53.590 --> 00:29:57.890
Since you have all proven resistant
to individualized hammer therapy,

00:29:58.061 --> 00:30:01.053
I now prescribe group therapy.

00:30:07.471 --> 00:30:09.439
Everything must be clean, very clean.

00:30:09.540 --> 00:30:12.703
That's why the dog had to die.
He was a dirty dog. Dirty, dirty.

00:30:12.810 --> 00:30:15.301
Also, that boy, Elroy. Dirty, dirty.

00:30:15.412 --> 00:30:18.313
Who would like to share their feelings?

00:30:18.415 --> 00:30:20.883
- I feel unappreciated at work.
- What?

00:30:20.984 --> 00:30:23.748
- I can barely understand you.
- I said I feel...

00:30:23.854 --> 00:30:25.344
Change places.

00:30:28.025 --> 00:30:32.826
Well, well. Looks like old Roberto
is the focus of attention now.

00:30:33.430 --> 00:30:34.863
Stop looking at me.

00:30:37.734 --> 00:30:39.429
Calm down, Roberto.

00:30:39.536 --> 00:30:41.629
Tell us about your childhood.

00:30:41.738 --> 00:30:44.935
I was designed by a team of engineers
attempting to build

00:30:45.042 --> 00:30:48.739
an insane robot. But it seems they failed.

00:30:49.546 --> 00:30:51.036
Actually...

00:30:53.584 --> 00:30:57.577
Look, we have to accept the fact
that we all have a serious problem.

00:30:57.688 --> 00:31:01.124
And if we ever wanna get out of here,
the first step is to admit it.

00:31:01.225 --> 00:31:02.283
- Amen.
- Good, Bender.

00:31:02.392 --> 00:31:03.381
- That's right.
- Yes.

00:31:03.493 --> 00:31:05.825
There's a band of river trolls
living in the moat,

00:31:05.929 --> 00:31:08.591
and they may have no intention
of letting us out of this castle,

00:31:08.699 --> 00:31:12.465
unless we hand over
the Golden Scepter of Zanthor.

00:31:12.569 --> 00:31:14.628
Say what? Dude's crazy.

00:31:14.771 --> 00:31:18.366
- Bender, please, try to...
- I know not of this Bender.

00:31:18.475 --> 00:31:20.443
I am Titanius Inglesmith,

00:31:20.544 --> 00:31:22.136
fancy man of Cornwood.

00:31:22.246 --> 00:31:24.908
You are suffering a breakdown. Now stop.

00:31:25.015 --> 00:31:26.107
Hammer time.

00:31:29.319 --> 00:31:33.847
I'm in your seat.
I forgot we had changed places.

00:31:33.957 --> 00:31:35.447
Change places.

00:31:39.396 --> 00:31:41.125
Good news, everyone!

00:31:41.231 --> 00:31:44.098
- You perfected dog mascara?
- Far from it.

00:31:44.201 --> 00:31:46.533
If you ask me, they look like
a bunch of hookers.

00:31:46.637 --> 00:31:50.767
But what I have invented is a means
of locating the missing crystal.

00:31:52.142 --> 00:31:56.442
When I push this button, the crystal
will emit a high-frequency stink.

00:31:56.546 --> 00:31:57.672
Hurray!

00:31:58.615 --> 00:32:02.176
There. Now, with any luck
I'll detect it with my smelling aid.

00:32:03.954 --> 00:32:09.756
I just pray to all powerful Atheismo
that we find it before Mom does.

00:32:10.193 --> 00:32:12.991
- Do you smell the crystal, Professor?
- No, damn it!

00:32:13.096 --> 00:32:16.463
Just the alluring scent of Obsession
for spaniels.

00:32:23.206 --> 00:32:27.302
- Dude. Who whipped an egger?
- He who smelled it, dealt it.

00:32:27.411 --> 00:32:30.073
Yeah? Well, he who denied it, supplied it.

00:32:30.180 --> 00:32:33.445
Well, he who articulated it, particulated it.

00:32:33.550 --> 00:32:35.950
Well, he who refuted it, tooted it.

00:32:37.587 --> 00:32:38.884
Stalemate.

00:32:41.725 --> 00:32:44.819
Jesus craps. The anti-backwards crystal.

00:32:44.928 --> 00:32:45.895
Ow!

00:32:46.596 --> 00:32:49.531
- Sorry?
- Relax, it's not your fault.

00:32:49.633 --> 00:32:51.601
I can't believe it still exists.

00:32:51.702 --> 00:32:53.829
Google the hell out of that skanker.

00:32:58.241 --> 00:33:00.300
Planet-sucking-Express?

00:33:00.410 --> 00:33:03.208
Of course.
How could I have been so dumb?

00:33:04.381 --> 00:33:05.575
With that crystal,

00:33:05.682 --> 00:33:09.174
Farnsworth could completely destroy
my dark matter empire.

00:33:09.286 --> 00:33:13.655
I underestimated that sagging
old bag of bones and gonads.

00:33:13.757 --> 00:33:16.317
- Is that man bad?
- Very bad, Igner.

00:33:16.560 --> 00:33:19.927
And that's why I need you three to go
steal the anti-crystal away from him.

00:33:20.030 --> 00:33:23.727
But be careful.
You'll need all your stoogely cunning.

00:33:31.008 --> 00:33:33.203
- Exterminators.
- Oh, great.

00:33:33.310 --> 00:33:36.006
What do we got?
Wall gophers? Toilet snails?

00:33:36.113 --> 00:33:39.048
No, I'm afraid you've got owls.
Over there, see?

00:33:40.817 --> 00:33:41.806
Ow!

00:33:41.918 --> 00:33:43.613
Dump the bag, you nitwit.

00:33:44.454 --> 00:33:46.422
- Hey, watch it.
- Quiet, you.

00:33:46.523 --> 00:33:47.490
Ow!

00:33:48.358 --> 00:33:50.826
I was looking over there for a long time
but I didn't see any...

00:33:50.927 --> 00:33:54.124
Oh, there they are. Gross.

00:33:54.231 --> 00:33:57.394
We've got to act fast.
Larry, get out the geigersniffer.

00:33:57.501 --> 00:34:00.334
I don't know, Walt.
You're just gonna hit me with it.

00:34:00.437 --> 00:34:02.564
No. I'm going to hit you with this.

00:34:07.577 --> 00:34:11.104
- Those three exterminators are hilarious.
- Really?

00:34:11.214 --> 00:34:13.205
- I don't think so.
- Me, neither.

00:34:13.316 --> 00:34:15.580
Now, Sex and the City, that's funny.

00:34:16.553 --> 00:34:20.819
After wandering aimlessly
in the swamp, you suddenly...

00:34:20.924 --> 00:34:23.119
Wander aimlessly in the swamp.

00:34:28.131 --> 00:34:29.860
There it is.

00:34:31.034 --> 00:34:34.526
Excuse you.
As you apparently didn't notice,

00:34:34.638 --> 00:34:37.698
we're trying to traverse
the Quagmire of Slogdonia.

00:34:37.808 --> 00:34:41.107
I'm sorry, little boy.
You see, we're owl exterminators.

00:34:41.211 --> 00:34:42.576
We are owl...

00:34:42.679 --> 00:34:44.078
Ow!

00:34:44.347 --> 00:34:47.578
And what we have here is an owl egg

00:34:47.684 --> 00:34:50.778
that's about to hatch into an owl larva.

00:34:50.887 --> 00:34:52.946
So, if you don't mind,
we'll just take this and...

00:34:53.056 --> 00:34:55.251
What are you, stupid?

00:34:55.358 --> 00:34:59.624
That's a dodecahedral crystal I found
hidden in the downstairs walrus tank.

00:34:59.729 --> 00:35:02.459
And I wrote numbers on it
so we could use it as a D12.

00:35:02.566 --> 00:35:04.193
'Cause I have the best handwriting.

00:35:04.301 --> 00:35:05.666
- Do not.
- Do too.

00:35:05.769 --> 00:35:07.134
- Do not.
- Do too.

00:35:08.338 --> 00:35:10.169
You win this round.

00:35:10.273 --> 00:35:11.797
What's going on here?

00:35:11.908 --> 00:35:14.206
We're owl exterminators.

00:35:15.245 --> 00:35:18.772
Then you won't have any problem
exterminating this owl.

00:35:29.426 --> 00:35:30.552
Please!

00:35:36.233 --> 00:35:38.224
My anti-backwards crystal.

00:35:39.803 --> 00:35:41.293
So it's you three.

00:35:41.404 --> 00:35:45.534
I should have known Mom would send
her brainless brood to do her dirty work.

00:35:46.376 --> 00:35:49.174
- Walt, the leader among imbeciles.
- Hey!

00:35:49.279 --> 00:35:51.076
They resent that.

00:35:51.181 --> 00:35:54.014
Larry, the sniveling middle child.

00:35:54.117 --> 00:35:55.516
Sorry. Thank you.

00:35:56.653 --> 00:36:01.249
And you, Igner. The evil I could tolerate,
but the stupidity...

00:36:03.059 --> 00:36:06.551
- We're owl exterminators.
- Good God.

00:36:06.663 --> 00:36:09.632
Just knowing we're in the same genus
makes me embarrassed

00:36:09.733 --> 00:36:11.564
to call myself homo.

00:36:13.069 --> 00:36:16.903
Now, get out and tell Mom
thanks for the crystal.

00:36:24.915 --> 00:36:26.507
Thanks for the crystal.

00:36:34.591 --> 00:36:36.024
There. The repairs are complete.

00:36:37.194 --> 00:36:38.252
Let's go, already.

00:36:38.428 --> 00:36:42.091
We've got to infiltrate
Mom's dark matter mine, now.

00:36:42.199 --> 00:36:43.996
How do you start this thing?

00:36:45.802 --> 00:36:48.771
Good lord, woman.
Can you move any slower?

00:36:49.406 --> 00:36:52.102
Rake up some dark matter
and top off the tank.

00:36:52.209 --> 00:36:55.406
Well, there isn't any dark matter.
Nibbler hasn't pooped at all.

00:36:55.512 --> 00:36:58.276
And he ate a whole family
of koalas last night.

00:36:58.381 --> 00:37:01.475
Nibbler! Nibbler!

00:37:01.585 --> 00:37:05.783
I'm not interested in the whereabouts
of your cutesy-fruitsy space rat.

00:37:05.889 --> 00:37:08.357
The only thing that matters right now
is this crystal.

00:37:08.458 --> 00:37:09.425
Ow!

00:37:09.559 --> 00:37:11.686
And be careful with that crystal.

00:37:23.707 --> 00:37:25.140
Death to ogres!

00:37:26.409 --> 00:37:29.435
Even relaxation therapy has failed.

00:37:31.815 --> 00:37:33.874
Diagnosis, insanity.

00:37:33.984 --> 00:37:36.817
Nurse, schedule a robotomy for Bender.

00:37:36.920 --> 00:37:39.480
Yes, Doctor.
I'll get the tools from the shed.

00:37:39.589 --> 00:37:43.889
It's a very painful procedure.
So until then, just try to relax.

00:38:08.318 --> 00:38:11.549
- What are you laughing at?
- Your laugh.

00:38:11.655 --> 00:38:14.988
- It's just so infectious.
- So's herpes. Now, shut up!

00:38:15.091 --> 00:38:17.423
You and Walt,
lead the killbots to the surface

00:38:17.527 --> 00:38:19.825
and blow Farnsworth out of the sky.

00:38:19.929 --> 00:38:20.987
What about Igner?

00:38:21.097 --> 00:38:22.257
That hairless ape?

00:38:22.365 --> 00:38:27.234
I swear. When he came out, I flipped a coin
whether to keep him or the after-birth.

00:38:27.337 --> 00:38:30.397
Yes, Mother.
You told that story at his graduation.

00:38:30.507 --> 00:38:33.032
I'm afraid he can't be trusted
on this mission.

00:38:33.143 --> 00:38:37.546
You see, there is a terrible secret
about Igner I've never told anyone.

00:38:37.647 --> 00:38:39.046
And here it is.

00:39:00.804 --> 00:39:03.637
- Continue returning fire.
- What?

00:39:05.241 --> 00:39:08.472
- What did they say?
- I don't know. I can't hear a thing.

00:39:08.578 --> 00:39:10.671
Hey, what's everybody talking about?

00:39:26.930 --> 00:39:28.727
Mayday! Mayday!

00:39:29.299 --> 00:39:32.666
Oh, God. I cannot believe
this is the best plan I could come up with.

00:39:43.646 --> 00:39:45.637
We weren't actually in the ship.

00:39:49.786 --> 00:39:52.914
Okay, team, these red-hot,
razor-sharp fans

00:39:53.022 --> 00:39:55.183
are the only safe way into the mine.

00:39:55.892 --> 00:39:56.984
Ladies first.

00:40:03.366 --> 00:40:06.426
Whew! That blade missed me
by the skin of my pants.

00:40:16.479 --> 00:40:18.913
- Maintenance shaft 7 serving...
- Shut your mouth.

00:40:19.015 --> 00:40:21.074
I'm just talking about the shaft.

00:40:24.587 --> 00:40:28.455
- Jeez. Doesn't that shock collar hurt?
- Actually, feels kind of good.

00:40:28.558 --> 00:40:32.460
I guess I'm starting to associate it
with the pleasure of beating people up.

00:40:50.980 --> 00:40:52.379
We shot them down, Mother.

00:40:52.482 --> 00:40:55.076
The intruders never even got to Sector 1.

00:40:55.185 --> 00:40:58.586
Intruders in Sector 15.
Intruders in Sector 15.

00:40:58.688 --> 00:40:59.677
Ugh...

00:40:59.789 --> 00:41:03.156
Sometimes I don't know why
I even bother to slap you.

00:41:05.829 --> 00:41:09.265
- All killbots to Sector 15.
- What did she say?

00:41:09.365 --> 00:41:10.764
What did you say?

00:41:20.910 --> 00:41:23.674
There are so many killbots behind us,
I can't count them all.

00:41:23.780 --> 00:41:25.475
Three, I think.

00:41:28.852 --> 00:41:30.080
We're trapped.

00:41:30.653 --> 00:41:32.678
The main pit must be in here.

00:41:32.789 --> 00:41:35.758
I'm detecting vast quantities
of dark matter.

00:41:35.859 --> 00:41:38.419
Step aside turkey-neck.
I think I know the code.

00:41:43.132 --> 00:41:45.692
We're in. We're in the heart of the mine.

00:41:45.802 --> 00:41:48.396
The very source of all Mom's wealth and...

00:42:04.521 --> 00:42:07.149
My God! This isn't a crap mine.

00:42:07.257 --> 00:42:08.588
It's a crap farm.

00:42:11.361 --> 00:42:13.158
Is there really so much of a distinction?

00:42:13.263 --> 00:42:15.322
- I mean...
- Leela, it's me, Nibbler.

00:42:16.566 --> 00:42:20.434
Oh, my God, you look horrible, Nibbler.
I think I'm going to vomit.

00:42:20.537 --> 00:42:21.799
Nibbler is over there.

00:42:21.905 --> 00:42:25.136
Oh, sorry. Nibbler.

00:42:25.241 --> 00:42:27.937
Oh, my poor little snuzzy-wuzzams.

00:42:28.044 --> 00:42:29.909
Are they treating you okay?

00:42:30.013 --> 00:42:33.505
No, they are force-feeding us
so we poop more dark matter.

00:42:33.616 --> 00:42:34.583
It's horrible.

00:42:42.659 --> 00:42:43.717
Those are good.

00:42:43.826 --> 00:42:45.088
You've got to help us.

00:42:45.194 --> 00:42:47.253
- Help us!
- Help us, for God's sakes!

00:42:52.468 --> 00:42:56.871
- Nibbler made a bo-bo.
- Yes, but not on my terms.

00:42:56.973 --> 00:43:01.307
I will not be treated like...
Hey, wait, aren't you amazed I can speak?

00:43:01.411 --> 00:43:05.211
Well, actually, no. You forgot to blank
our memories after you spoke last time.

00:43:05.315 --> 00:43:07.476
You mean you've known I was sentient?

00:43:07.584 --> 00:43:11.179
Then why did you let me eat Friskies
and make bo-bo in a litter box?

00:43:11.287 --> 00:43:14.256
- Well, you're cuter that way.
- Cute as a baby's buttocks.

00:43:14.357 --> 00:43:17.485
So what happened?
How did Mom capture all you Nibblonians?

00:43:18.828 --> 00:43:25.290
It all began 36 years ago... Now!
On the planet Virgon 6...

00:43:26.536 --> 00:43:28.231
It was a veritable Eden,

00:43:28.338 --> 00:43:31.136
brimming with unique
and irreplaceable species.

00:43:32.508 --> 00:43:36.000
Most of which were delicious.

00:43:36.112 --> 00:43:39.912
I was supreme fuzzler
of a Nibblonian scientific outpost.

00:43:40.016 --> 00:43:43.679
It was paradise, until they came.

00:43:50.560 --> 00:43:52.790
One of your duke ships struck dark matter,

00:43:52.895 --> 00:43:55.523
little realizing it was not a natural deposit,

00:43:55.632 --> 00:43:58.795
but rather centuries
of Nibblonian fecal material.

00:43:58.901 --> 00:44:02.860
Wow, the big fecal enchilada.
Anyone else hungry?

00:44:06.576 --> 00:44:09.067
The duke contracted
a ruthless businesswoman

00:44:09.178 --> 00:44:11.305
to spearhead the mining operation.

00:44:11.581 --> 00:44:14.607
- Let me guess. Mom?
- The very same.

00:44:14.717 --> 00:44:15.843
Can I also guess Mom?

00:44:17.654 --> 00:44:20.748
To reduce cost
she started a new enterprise,

00:44:20.857 --> 00:44:22.347
Mom 's Friendly Robots,

00:44:22.458 --> 00:44:24.483
to build robot slaves.

00:44:24.594 --> 00:44:27.927
Remember this was back in the days
before Robot Lincoln.

00:44:28.031 --> 00:44:30.522
- Faster, faster!
- I'm going exactly

00:44:30.633 --> 00:44:33.659
- as fast as you built me to go.
- Wise guy, huh?

00:44:36.506 --> 00:44:37.473
Ow!

00:44:37.740 --> 00:44:41.267
Eventually, the planet was mined
down to a hollow shell

00:44:41.377 --> 00:44:43.971
and my people were forced to evacuate.

00:44:46.916 --> 00:44:50.818
Alas, I had eaten a day-old
swinosaur for lunch.

00:44:50.920 --> 00:44:55.948
And while doing some evacuating
of my own, I was left behind.

00:44:57.527 --> 00:44:59.654
So, that's where it comes from.

00:44:59.762 --> 00:45:03.459
We may have a whole new source
of dark matter on our hands.

00:45:03.633 --> 00:45:05.032
Ew!

00:45:09.238 --> 00:45:12.002
As it turned out, I was the lucky one.

00:45:12.108 --> 00:45:15.703
Unbeknownst to me, Mom captured
my colleagues and enslaved them here

00:45:15.812 --> 00:45:18.337
in this crap farm.

00:45:21.451 --> 00:45:26.320
There's nothing to do but eat and crap,
eat and crap. It's like visiting my parents.

00:45:26.422 --> 00:45:31.325
As for me, I emerged
from behind the bush of many uses

00:45:31.427 --> 00:45:35.887
to find I had been left behind.
I was doomed, doomed.

00:45:35.998 --> 00:45:37.090
Hello, there.

00:45:37.200 --> 00:45:40.692
Startled, my cuteness reflex kicked in.

00:45:44.407 --> 00:45:45.840
I'll call him Nibbler.

00:45:45.942 --> 00:45:48.672
A silly name
for a high-ranking fuzzler.

00:45:48.778 --> 00:45:51.975
But, hey, I was glad to be rescued.

00:45:56.185 --> 00:45:59.018
But then, how did you end up here
with the others?

00:45:59.122 --> 00:46:02.216
I was kidnapped yesterday
by Mom's vile sons,

00:46:02.325 --> 00:46:04.589
in their moronic disguises.

00:46:04.694 --> 00:46:07.026
I was an owl exterminator.

00:46:09.465 --> 00:46:14.198
- Do you have the crysal?
- It's pronounced "crystal," you lump.

00:46:15.838 --> 00:46:17.328
Go, run fast.

00:46:27.316 --> 00:46:28.613
Did you see anyone?

00:46:28.718 --> 00:46:31.414
- Me?
- Yes, you. You're the only one here.

00:46:31.521 --> 00:46:35.184
If I'm the only one here,
then how could I see anyone?

00:46:35.291 --> 00:46:37.259
- He's got a point, Walt.
- So does my knee.

00:46:43.399 --> 00:46:46.197
This wouldn't be so bad
if it weren't for the chickens.

00:46:51.808 --> 00:46:54.834
Don't worry, those clamps
are for my own protection.

00:46:54.944 --> 00:46:57.174
Do you know where you are, Bender?

00:46:57.280 --> 00:47:01.376
Sure do, I'm in the magical land of
Cornwood, frolicking with wenches.

00:47:01.484 --> 00:47:04.783
Close, you're in the loony bin
for a robotomy.

00:47:04.887 --> 00:47:09.051
I will begin by drilling through the eye
to access the frontal processor.

00:47:11.093 --> 00:47:15.496
- Can't you just use the access panel?
- Either way is fine.

00:47:15.598 --> 00:47:17.793
Does anyone else smell
burning dragon beak?

00:47:30.213 --> 00:47:34.980
Wherever you are, Farnsworth,
my boys will find you.

00:47:35.084 --> 00:47:36.244
They've eluded us, Mother.

00:47:36.352 --> 00:47:38.513
But rest assured,
we've already slapped each other,

00:47:38.621 --> 00:47:40.589
so there's no need to...

00:47:40.690 --> 00:47:43.921
You'll thank me some day
when you are slapping your own kids.

00:47:44.026 --> 00:47:46.017
I know Farnsworth's game.

00:47:46.128 --> 00:47:49.063
He is going to try to poke
his clammy old crystal

00:47:49.165 --> 00:47:52.532
- at my hot fiery crystal.
- Mom!

00:47:52.835 --> 00:47:55.929
If the crystals get within six inches
of each other... Wham!

00:47:56.038 --> 00:47:58.598
All my dark matter will be worthless.

00:48:08.618 --> 00:48:09.949
Get them!

00:48:13.823 --> 00:48:17.418
Keep going, Professor.
I'll take care of the ditz brothers.

00:48:22.798 --> 00:48:23.992
Ooh.

00:48:24.100 --> 00:48:27.069
- That feels good.
- Oh, for crying out...

00:48:32.975 --> 00:48:36.308
Oh, the freaking battery's dead.
Walt, where's the charger?

00:48:36.412 --> 00:48:38.812
In the hardware drawer, Mother.

00:48:41.717 --> 00:48:44.049
Damn tangled mess of wires.

00:48:44.153 --> 00:48:47.782
We're almost there.
The crystals are beginning to engorge.

00:49:05.975 --> 00:49:09.308
I can't quite reach.

00:49:09.946 --> 00:49:13.177
Fry, grab onto my easy-fit waistband.

00:49:17.286 --> 00:49:19.186
Just a few more inches.

00:49:19.288 --> 00:49:22.416
Come on, really wedgie it on in there.

00:49:27.430 --> 00:49:30.194
So, that's why they call me the Catman.

00:49:31.033 --> 00:49:33.058
Nobody move. I've found the charger.

00:49:34.337 --> 00:49:37.204
Hang on. I'm on it. Okay, there!

00:49:37.306 --> 00:49:38.933
Save us, Catman.

00:49:39.041 --> 00:49:42.135
It's over, Hubert.
Give me the anti-backwards crystal.

00:49:42.244 --> 00:49:43.438
Never!

00:49:51.654 --> 00:49:53.019
Oh, bravo.

00:49:53.122 --> 00:49:55.750
You're in a crap-harvesting factory, genius.

00:49:55.858 --> 00:49:57.985
Walt! Larry! Start harvesting.

00:49:59.295 --> 00:50:00.762
No!

00:50:05.434 --> 00:50:08.926
I will now delicately
jerk out your imagination,

00:50:09.038 --> 00:50:11.871
severing fantasy's grip
on your nerd-circuit.

00:50:15.077 --> 00:50:18.843
Cornwood!

00:50:21.050 --> 00:50:24.952
Illogical. Illogical. Computational overload.

00:50:25.054 --> 00:50:26.783
But, Doctor, I love you.

00:50:31.260 --> 00:50:32.591
Oh, what now?

00:50:48.444 --> 00:50:50.173
This is crazy. Ow!

00:50:50.713 --> 00:50:54.513
- What the... You okay, Leela?
- Yeah, I think so.

00:50:56.819 --> 00:50:59.049
Wait a second. Is there something
different about your hooves?

00:51:00.256 --> 00:51:03.054
Oh, Lord. I'm half-horse and half-naked.

00:51:03.159 --> 00:51:04.888
Where the hell are we, hell?

00:51:10.966 --> 00:51:13.958
- Bender?
- I know not of this Bender.

00:51:14.070 --> 00:51:19.474
I'm Titanius Inglesmith.
Welcome to Cornwood!

00:51:30.586 --> 00:51:33.282
Wretched peasants, put aside your cares

00:51:33.389 --> 00:51:37.655
and feast on the succulent flesh
of the roast munchkin!

00:51:40.329 --> 00:51:42.661
Care for a slice of scroto?

00:51:43.099 --> 00:51:46.193
- That's his name, right?
- 'Tis also that, sir.

00:51:46.302 --> 00:51:49.863
We're honored this eve
by a visit from my friends of old,

00:51:49.972 --> 00:51:52.099
Frydo and Legola.

00:51:52.208 --> 00:51:55.006
So let the dwarves do their gay dance

00:51:55.111 --> 00:51:58.342
and let the gnomes
play their sissy piccolos.

00:52:04.019 --> 00:52:06.146
Dance! Dance, you little freaks.

00:52:07.289 --> 00:52:08.483
Faster.

00:52:09.558 --> 00:52:10.923
Faster!

00:52:14.697 --> 00:52:17.063
- My ankle!
- To the kitchen with him!

00:52:17.766 --> 00:52:19.734
Wait! Wait! Wait! I do impressions.

00:52:19.835 --> 00:52:21.735
Behold! The swamp hag.

00:52:21.837 --> 00:52:24.829
Get out of my swamp, you kids!

00:52:24.940 --> 00:52:26.532
Don't let him get too crispy.

00:52:28.844 --> 00:52:32.211
- Lord Inglesmith.
- You have ridden hard, noble squire.

00:52:32.314 --> 00:52:34.976
May I offer you a horn of ale
and a shank of dwarf?

00:52:35.084 --> 00:52:37.917
'Tis dire news, sire. Dark riders approach.

00:52:39.155 --> 00:52:41.419
You shall be handsomely rewarded,
sir knight.

00:52:41.524 --> 00:52:43.219
We ride at once!

00:52:46.629 --> 00:52:47.994
Oops!

00:52:49.798 --> 00:52:52.665
Frydo! Saddle up that trusty steed.

00:53:00.943 --> 00:53:03.605
What's happening?
And why am I enjoying it so much?

00:53:06.048 --> 00:53:07.447
Foul beast-bags!

00:53:07.550 --> 00:53:09.279
Meet thy doom!

00:53:14.690 --> 00:53:15.918
Follow me.

00:53:21.664 --> 00:53:25.361
- Damn thee, Ignus.
- Well, you said to follow you.

00:53:25.467 --> 00:53:27.332
Well, now I say follow this!

00:53:31.373 --> 00:53:34.740
- The die of power! He's rolling it.
- Oh, no!

00:53:36.879 --> 00:53:38.574
I'm back...

00:53:40.115 --> 00:53:41.514
Seven.

00:53:44.987 --> 00:53:46.955
"Banish foes"? Cool.

00:53:47.056 --> 00:53:48.921
No! No!

00:53:54.563 --> 00:53:57.623
I got to say, I had no idea
the die of power was so powerful.

00:53:57.733 --> 00:53:59.667
Did you have any idea of...

00:53:59.969 --> 00:54:03.234
Get out of my swamp, you kids!

00:54:06.709 --> 00:54:09.803
I can't believe I'm saying this,
but that was really exciting.

00:54:09.912 --> 00:54:11.573
I've never felt so alive.

00:54:13.849 --> 00:54:16.716
What else can we slay?
Is that a hobbit over there?

00:54:16.819 --> 00:54:19.014
No, that's a hobo and a rabbit.

00:54:19.121 --> 00:54:20.918
But they're making a hobbit.

00:54:22.524 --> 00:54:26.324
Thank God, an outhouse.
I can't hold it in much longer.

00:54:26.428 --> 00:54:28.521
And by it, I mean my entrails.

00:54:28.631 --> 00:54:30.599
Hush! This be no outhouse,

00:54:30.699 --> 00:54:33.600
but the lair of the great wizard Grayfarn.

00:54:35.704 --> 00:54:38.502
- Who is it?
- 'Tis I, Titanius.

00:54:38.607 --> 00:54:39.835
Just a moment.

00:54:41.844 --> 00:54:45.541
Methinks the wizard be casting
a powerful spell, indeed.

00:54:48.217 --> 00:54:49.912
Come in! Come in!

00:54:51.487 --> 00:54:52.613
Yes.

00:54:52.721 --> 00:54:55.884
'Tis a powerful object in both our worlds.

00:54:55.991 --> 00:54:58.391
If you failed to destroy it in yours,

00:54:58.494 --> 00:55:01.952
perhaps you were brought here
that you might have a second chance.

00:55:02.064 --> 00:55:05.522
- So, this land is real?
- Oh, dreadfully real.

00:55:05.634 --> 00:55:07.932
If you die here, you'll really be dead.

00:55:08.037 --> 00:55:11.632
But instead of science,
we believe in crazy hocus-pocus.

00:55:11.740 --> 00:55:14.334
- It's like Kansas.
- God help us.

00:55:15.811 --> 00:55:21.113
Cornwood's troubles began
hundreds or perhaps millions of years ago.

00:55:21.517 --> 00:55:24.816
Deep in the Geysers of Gygax,
Momon herself

00:55:24.920 --> 00:55:29.380
injection-molded the dice of power
from the living plastic.

00:55:33.662 --> 00:55:35.095
Damn, these are hot.

00:55:36.999 --> 00:55:38.967
In our universe she's called Mom.

00:55:39.068 --> 00:55:42.060
In your universe,
are you taught not to interrupt?

00:55:42.171 --> 00:55:43.263
Evidently not.

00:55:43.372 --> 00:55:46.239
Anyway, Momon spawned
three rotten sons,

00:55:46.342 --> 00:55:48.936
whom you've already had
the displeasure of meeting.

00:55:49.278 --> 00:55:54.306
Waltazar, Larius, and the dumbest of all,
the halfwit Ignus,

00:55:54.616 --> 00:55:58.245
bastard son of Momon
and the brainless He-demon.

00:55:58.921 --> 00:56:01.754
Curse you, Momon, queen of all that is evil

00:56:01.857 --> 00:56:03.791
and not very good in bed.

00:56:03.892 --> 00:56:06.588
And I'm not just saying that
because she dumped me.

00:56:09.031 --> 00:56:12.262
Yes, I was once her consort.

00:56:12.368 --> 00:56:17.271
I was blinded by love,
and later, scorpion venom.

00:56:17.373 --> 00:56:18.340
I'm blind!

00:56:18.707 --> 00:56:21.232
But Momon has one weakness.

00:56:21.343 --> 00:56:23.903
She put too much of her power into this.

00:56:24.012 --> 00:56:26.708
The generalissimo of dice.

00:56:26.815 --> 00:56:29.750
Yeah? Well, bite my shiny metal face.

00:56:33.589 --> 00:56:35.557
Don't be foolish, Titanius.

00:56:35.657 --> 00:56:38.285
If you had paid attention
in freshman alchemy,

00:56:38.394 --> 00:56:40.555
instead of frequenting the bawdyhouse,

00:56:40.662 --> 00:56:43.358
you'd know
there's only one way to destroy it.

00:56:43.599 --> 00:56:46.898
In the boiling plastic
from which it was molded.

00:56:47.002 --> 00:56:49.732
Like that machine
that makes wax lions at the zoo.

00:56:49.838 --> 00:56:50.805
Quiet, you.

00:56:50.906 --> 00:56:54.398
We must infiltrate the Geysers of Gygax,

00:56:54.510 --> 00:56:57.411
the impenetrable stronghold of Momon.

00:56:59.648 --> 00:57:02.378
Impossible. Impossible, I say.

00:57:02.484 --> 00:57:06.284
No, Titanius.
For we maintain one advantage,

00:57:06.388 --> 00:57:09.118
the element of surprise.

00:57:31.480 --> 00:57:34.005
Verily, our quest has begun.

00:57:34.116 --> 00:57:35.174
Stop right there.

00:57:36.551 --> 00:57:37.677
Hermes?

00:57:39.087 --> 00:57:43.046
- He's a centaur like me.
- You wish.

00:57:43.158 --> 00:57:47.288
I am Hermaphrodite,
most beautiful of centaurs.

00:57:47.395 --> 00:57:50.364
Gaze upon me and weep at my loveliness.

00:57:51.032 --> 00:57:52.863
Very well.

00:57:52.968 --> 00:57:54.629
Loveliest of centaurs,

00:57:54.736 --> 00:57:57.466
we seek to end Momon's reign of evil.

00:57:57.572 --> 00:58:00.040
Have you stout fighters at your command?

00:58:00.142 --> 00:58:02.610
One thousand archers of truest aim.

00:58:03.678 --> 00:58:04.645
Fire.

00:58:06.648 --> 00:58:08.912
Hey guys, I forgot I had this pumpkin.

00:58:11.887 --> 00:58:14.355
I knew it. My people are mighty warriors.

00:58:14.456 --> 00:58:18.722
Our enemies will be like Swiss cheese
with blood coming out of the holes.

00:58:20.462 --> 00:58:23.954
- We centaurs are creatures of peace.
- Oh, Lord.

00:58:24.065 --> 00:58:27.728
Violence is never justified.
We shall not join your quest.

00:58:27.836 --> 00:58:30.600
And furthermore,
if mayhem be your intent,

00:58:30.705 --> 00:58:32.639
you may not cross our lands.

00:58:32.741 --> 00:58:34.265
- Or what?
- Or...

00:58:34.910 --> 00:58:37.674
Uh... Mmm?

00:58:40.649 --> 00:58:42.116
You may pass.

00:58:52.994 --> 00:58:54.256
We're not there, we're here.

00:58:54.362 --> 00:58:55.624
- No, this way.
- I mean, here.

00:59:11.680 --> 00:59:14.114
Thank you, kindly, Treedledum.

00:59:14.216 --> 00:59:18.414
Okey-doke. Anything else I can do?

00:59:22.724 --> 00:59:25.557
You know who I'm gonna miss?
That tree guy.

00:59:32.133 --> 00:59:36.832
Bad news, fancy men.
Momon's guards stand watch at the pass.

00:59:36.938 --> 00:59:40.066
'Tis as if she somehow anticipated us.

00:59:40.175 --> 00:59:42.803
And so our quest comes to an end.

00:59:42.911 --> 00:59:45.379
I only regret not giving up sooner.

00:59:46.414 --> 00:59:50.214
Fret not, Titanius.
For we still have one hope,

00:59:50.318 --> 00:59:52.183
the Cave of Hopelessness.

00:59:54.055 --> 00:59:55.682
Let me know how that turns out.

01:00:00.195 --> 01:00:03.892
Halt. Are you on the list?
I'm not seeing you on the list.

01:00:03.999 --> 01:00:07.162
- I'll split this doofus in half.
- Wait. I got it.

01:00:07.535 --> 01:00:11.266
Yeah. My cousin's in the band.
The band of merry men.

01:00:11.940 --> 01:00:16.639
Please, we were already in there.
I just need to go back for my coat.

01:00:25.420 --> 01:00:30.084
I am Gynecaladriel,
queen of the water nymphos.

01:00:30.191 --> 01:00:32.659
All right. I'll split this doofus in half.

01:00:32.761 --> 01:00:37.130
Stand aside, and I will use my powers
to overwhelm the guard.

01:00:43.938 --> 01:00:47.066
- Behold, the deed is done.
- Ho!

01:00:53.348 --> 01:00:57.512
Mr. Wizard, why is this place
called the Cave of Hopelessness?

01:00:57.619 --> 01:00:59.052
Oh, fear not, lad.

01:00:59.154 --> 01:01:03.250
'Tis named for its discoverer,
Reginald Hopelessness...

01:01:03.391 --> 01:01:04.358
Whew!

01:01:04.459 --> 01:01:08.259
...the first man to be eaten alive
by the Tunneling Horror.

01:01:11.433 --> 01:01:13.458
What's that? The Tunneling Horror?

01:01:13.568 --> 01:01:15.695
No, it's morks.

01:01:15.804 --> 01:01:17.795
- Mork. Hey, listen.
- Nanu, nanu. Shazbot.

01:01:17.906 --> 01:01:21.774
- Oh, God, no. They're so aggravating.
- Oh, fantastic.

01:01:22.444 --> 01:01:23.411
Nanu, nanu.

01:01:23.745 --> 01:01:25.372
Reality, what a concept.

01:01:29.617 --> 01:01:30.879
Fantastic.

01:01:35.790 --> 01:01:36.779
Mindy, Mindy, Mindy.

01:01:36.891 --> 01:01:38.859
- Shut up! Shut up!
- Oh, fantastic.

01:01:38.993 --> 01:01:40.255
Oh, fantastic. Oh, wonderful.

01:01:40.362 --> 01:01:43.058
Maybe it'll go away
if we just don't laugh at it.

01:01:43.164 --> 01:01:44.859
It doesn't.

01:01:45.633 --> 01:01:46.600
Nanu, nanu.

01:01:49.804 --> 01:01:50.771
Shazbot.

01:01:52.574 --> 01:01:56.533
Well, at least we didn't have to face
the tunneling whatchimacallit.

01:01:56.644 --> 01:01:57.611
Uh-oh.

01:01:59.414 --> 01:02:02.474
Enough already with the banging
and the swashbuckling.

01:02:08.156 --> 01:02:11.057
Oh, I'm gonna enjoy killing you.

01:02:12.193 --> 01:02:14.889
Watch where you're shooting that thing.

01:02:15.597 --> 01:02:18.657
Again?
What, am I talking to myself over here?

01:02:18.767 --> 01:02:20.564
Mutilate!

01:02:22.137 --> 01:02:25.538
Okay. Now, I'm getting a little mad even.

01:02:34.282 --> 01:02:37.080
I'll kill you and eat your heart,
you abomination.

01:02:43.525 --> 01:02:44.992
Don't make me laugh.

01:02:45.093 --> 01:02:48.324
The very idea that removing only
one of my two hearts could...

01:02:48.430 --> 01:02:50.557
Hey, what are you doing down there?

01:02:51.933 --> 01:02:53.423
Now, I'm dead.

01:02:55.770 --> 01:02:58.136
Leela, it's over. You killed him enough.

01:02:58.239 --> 01:03:01.174
I'm not taking any chances
with the Tunneling Horror.

01:03:01.776 --> 01:03:06.179
What? I'm not the Tunneling Horror.
I hate that guy.

01:03:06.281 --> 01:03:09.512
Always with the tunneling.
Anyway, I'm dead.

01:03:10.151 --> 01:03:12.676
So, you're just an innocent monster.

01:03:12.787 --> 01:03:14.880
Oh, God. What have I done?

01:03:16.925 --> 01:03:18.893
Oh! There he goes again.

01:03:25.900 --> 01:03:27.390
The Tunneling Horror!

01:03:30.038 --> 01:03:31.733
Grayfarn, what do we do?

01:03:33.541 --> 01:03:34.803
Do about what?

01:03:39.848 --> 01:03:42.715
Why aren't you killing it, Leela?
You love killing.

01:03:42.817 --> 01:03:45.115
No, no more killing.

01:03:45.220 --> 01:03:49.452
Oh! So, suddenly, Miss Goody Four-shoes
over here doesn't kill anymore.

01:03:49.557 --> 01:03:51.354
She killed me not five minutes ago.

01:03:51.459 --> 01:03:53.586
- What am I? Chopped liver?
- Shut up.

01:03:54.429 --> 01:03:57.455
- Stop chopping my liver.
- You're on your own.

01:03:57.565 --> 01:04:00.363
I refuse to hurt another living thing.

01:04:06.674 --> 01:04:10.166
All right.
I may be weak and I may be small,

01:04:10.278 --> 01:04:13.475
but I don't see
how I can possibly destroy that monster.

01:04:13.581 --> 01:04:15.742
Guess I'll just
huck whatever's in my pockets at him.

01:04:15.850 --> 01:04:17.249
At least I can say I tried.

01:04:17.352 --> 01:04:18.785
Any time now.

01:04:23.892 --> 01:04:26.793
The die of power.
I forgot to remember to roll it.

01:04:32.800 --> 01:04:34.358
Three.

01:04:36.838 --> 01:04:40.399
"Grow"? I don't see anything growing.
Everything is getting smaller.

01:04:43.912 --> 01:04:44.970
Ow.

01:04:45.079 --> 01:04:46.910
Wait a second. I'm big!

01:04:47.015 --> 01:04:50.348
In your face, everyone from middle school.
Especially, Jeremy.

01:05:03.798 --> 01:05:05.129
Wow, that was intense.

01:05:05.233 --> 01:05:08.225
- You guys got to try the die of power.
- I'll take a hit.

01:05:08.336 --> 01:05:10.566
Hands off the dodecalicious.

01:05:11.906 --> 01:05:15.637
Beware, Frydo. Don't be seduced.
Hang on a second.

01:05:18.012 --> 01:05:19.946
Resist the allure of the die.

01:05:20.048 --> 01:05:23.540
For to defeat Momon,
we must melt it in the super bombastic,

01:05:23.651 --> 01:05:26.245
bubbling plastic from whence it came.

01:05:30.058 --> 01:05:33.585
For to defeat Momon,
we must melt it in the super bombastic,

01:05:33.695 --> 01:05:36.289
bubbling plastic from whence it came.

01:05:36.631 --> 01:05:39.532
I send you to kill them
and they're not even maimed?

01:05:40.635 --> 01:05:44.435
That's what I get
for sending boys to do a mom's job.

01:05:44.539 --> 01:05:47.201
- Sorry, Mom.
- Sorry doesn't put heads on my table.

01:05:47.308 --> 01:05:49.401
Peaches.

01:05:49.510 --> 01:05:50.568
You're up.

01:05:56.050 --> 01:05:58.575
I like this part but I don't like...

01:06:05.393 --> 01:06:07.827
You are an able opponent, Hermaphrodite.

01:06:07.929 --> 01:06:09.954
But hear me well
when I posit that we must

01:06:10.064 --> 01:06:12.555
abhor violence in all its forms.

01:06:14.802 --> 01:06:17.032
I offer a dissenting opinion.

01:06:17.138 --> 01:06:18.127
Huh?

01:06:18.239 --> 01:06:21.504
For abhorring violence
is itself an act of violence

01:06:21.609 --> 01:06:24.077
and, therefore, to be abhorred.

01:06:29.117 --> 01:06:32.575
All bow before mighty Hermaphrodite.

01:06:33.287 --> 01:06:35.585
- Don't hurt me.
- I'm not here to hurt you.

01:06:35.690 --> 01:06:37.749
Or anything ever again.

01:06:37.859 --> 01:06:40.987
Please, teach me
the centaurs' ways of wimpiness.

01:06:41.095 --> 01:06:42.960
What do you offer in return?

01:06:46.834 --> 01:06:49.997
Chewy, Chewy, Chewy,
Chewy, Chewy, Chewy, Chewy

01:06:50.104 --> 01:06:54.040
Baby, always got a mouthful
of such sweet things to say

01:07:02.517 --> 01:07:03.882
Oh-ie little Chewy

01:07:03.985 --> 01:07:05.919
Don't know what you're doing to me

01:07:06.020 --> 01:07:09.046
But you're doing to me what I want you to

01:07:14.829 --> 01:07:18.959
Yes! We made it out
of that godforsaken cave.

01:07:19.067 --> 01:07:22.264
Now, what's the fastest way home?
Back through the cave?

01:07:22.370 --> 01:07:24.304
Ow! Ow!

01:07:30.344 --> 01:07:32.278
We're close now, my friends.

01:07:32.380 --> 01:07:37.249
So close, I can practically feel
the heat of the fiery molten plastic.

01:07:37.351 --> 01:07:40.286
- You're standing in the fire.
- Oh, my.

01:07:41.789 --> 01:07:45.953
Alas, our path is blocked
by Momon's army of evil.

01:07:46.060 --> 01:07:48.551
As well as her navy of moral dubiousness.

01:07:48.663 --> 01:07:49.789
Wait a second.

01:07:49.897 --> 01:07:52.457
Mayhaps we might
raise an army of our own.

01:07:52.567 --> 01:07:55.001
We're but
an hour's ride from Wipe Castle.

01:07:55.103 --> 01:07:57.128
Of course. Wipe Castle.

01:07:57.238 --> 01:08:01.436
And while we're there, we can get
some of those greasy little dwarf burgers.

01:08:01.609 --> 01:08:03.634
Ooh! I love those.

01:08:03.745 --> 01:08:06.179
You can eat like eight of them
without gaining any weight,

01:08:06.280 --> 01:08:07.770
because of all the diarrhea.

01:08:07.882 --> 01:08:10.214
Sleep deep, fair snoozles.

01:08:10.318 --> 01:08:13.412
At dawn, we ride for Wipe Castle.

01:08:16.958 --> 01:08:18.425
Quiet, Frydo.

01:08:25.600 --> 01:08:27.568
We've got them now.

01:08:27.668 --> 01:08:31.604
- Send all our forces against Wipe Castle.
- Right away, Mother.

01:08:31.706 --> 01:08:33.731
I'll just leave a small contingent behind
in case...

01:08:33.841 --> 01:08:37.902
- I said, everything. Peaches!
- I'm in the tub.

01:08:38.012 --> 01:08:41.038
Waltazar,
you and Larius shall lead the assault.

01:08:41.149 --> 01:08:42.275
What about Ignus?

01:08:42.383 --> 01:08:44.908
I'm afraid
he can't be trusted on this mission.

01:08:45.019 --> 01:08:47.817
You see, there is a terrible secret
about Ignus

01:08:47.922 --> 01:08:49.890
I've never told anyone.

01:08:49.991 --> 01:08:51.515
And here it is.

01:09:00.434 --> 01:09:03.130
It's a good day to be evil.

01:09:11.846 --> 01:09:14.337
Oh, put a towel on, for crap's sake.

01:09:22.490 --> 01:09:26.483
They all wants it.
They wants the dodecalicious.

01:09:26.594 --> 01:09:30.223
Tell you what,
you want to defend a magic artifact,

01:09:30.331 --> 01:09:32.356
and I mean, defend it good,

01:09:32.466 --> 01:09:35.264
then what you need is a top-quality knife.

01:09:35.369 --> 01:09:36.859
Me is listening.

01:09:37.004 --> 01:09:41.907
The Eviscerator is one of the finest,
if not the finest,

01:09:42.009 --> 01:09:44.443
tactical folder on the market today.

01:09:44.545 --> 01:09:50.006
We're talking 440 stainless,
quick release and... I don't believe this.

01:09:50.117 --> 01:09:52.984
Is this a stag horn handle at this price?

01:09:53.087 --> 01:09:56.056
- It is, yeah. It's a stag horn.
- At this price?

01:09:56.157 --> 01:09:58.387
You have got to be kidding me.

01:09:58.492 --> 01:10:01.188
That's got to be some kind of mistake,
right there.

01:10:01.295 --> 01:10:03.490
Now, you folks at home,
I know what you're thinking.

01:10:03.598 --> 01:10:06.089
You're thinking, that can't be stag horn.

01:10:06.200 --> 01:10:08.566
It's got to be the cheaper manticore horn.

01:10:08.669 --> 01:10:11.035
But, I've got the specs right here
and I'll tell you what,

01:10:11.138 --> 01:10:15.040
- this is the real deal.
- Unbelievable.

01:10:15.142 --> 01:10:17.269
It is unbelievable. That's exactly what it is.

01:10:17.378 --> 01:10:19.903
I mean, this is...
I have no words to describe this deal.

01:10:20.014 --> 01:10:22.608
Honestly, have you ever seen
stag horn at this price?

01:10:22.717 --> 01:10:25.481
No, no, I don't believe I ever have.

01:10:25.586 --> 01:10:29.955
1101-1816 is the item number on this one.

01:10:30.057 --> 01:10:32.321
You know what, we're gonna have to
put a clock on this deal, folks.

01:10:32.426 --> 01:10:34.860
Two minutes. Can I get a clock
at two minutes up there?

01:10:34.962 --> 01:10:35.929
Two minutes at most.

01:10:36.063 --> 01:10:37.826
Honestly,
I'd be surprised if they last that long.

01:10:37.932 --> 01:10:40.730
Oh, I'd be very surprised, shocked really.

01:10:40.835 --> 01:10:42.962
Now, I know the lines are busy, people,

01:10:43.070 --> 01:10:47.268
but keep dialing in if you want
a truly exceptional knife

01:10:47.375 --> 01:10:49.969
to slice up your friends in their sleep.

01:11:07.161 --> 01:11:09.493
He tried to murder me. He tried...

01:11:09.597 --> 01:11:11.565
Oh, cool. Is that the stag horn?

01:11:22.243 --> 01:11:26.873
Alas, Frydo's weakness
was no match for the die's strength.

01:11:26.981 --> 01:11:30.382
We can only hope he forges on
alone to the Geysers.

01:11:30.484 --> 01:11:32.452
I can hope my ass is made of ice-cream

01:11:32.553 --> 01:11:34.817
but that don't make me
a hot fudge sundae.

01:11:34.922 --> 01:11:38.085
As for us,
we must press on to Wipe Castle,

01:11:38.192 --> 01:11:41.923
though the journey be long
and I fear I may not live to see it.

01:11:42.029 --> 01:11:43.018
There it is!

01:11:56.477 --> 01:11:58.138
They's following us's.

01:11:58.245 --> 01:12:02.545
You know, you talk like that, it's gonna
cost you points at a job interview.

01:12:02.650 --> 01:12:03.878
What does it wants?

01:12:03.985 --> 01:12:06.783
First of all, I resent being called "it."

01:12:06.887 --> 01:12:08.912
I prefer jerkhole or simply...

01:12:10.091 --> 01:12:12.958
Second, I thought I could help you
destroy the die, maybe.

01:12:13.160 --> 01:12:16.721
Yes, yes, please help me.
The die is tearing me apart.

01:12:16.831 --> 01:12:18.458
No, it's not. We're having a nice time.

01:12:18.566 --> 01:12:19.897
Shut up. You shut up.

01:12:20.001 --> 01:12:21.730
S'all right? S'all right.

01:12:21.836 --> 01:12:23.064
Help me!

01:12:23.904 --> 01:12:27.032
Get out of my swamp, you kids!

01:12:39.620 --> 01:12:41.918
Now, before your audience with the king,

01:12:42.023 --> 01:12:44.548
there's a shocking fact
you best know about him.

01:12:44.658 --> 01:12:47.126
Enough blabbety-blab! Open the doors.

01:12:48.662 --> 01:12:50.152
What, ho?

01:12:50.264 --> 01:12:53.495
We bring ill tidings, o fanciest of men.

01:12:53.601 --> 01:12:55.933
Momon's reach nears the die of power.

01:12:56.037 --> 01:12:59.700
And should she obtain it,
she will then have the entire basic set.

01:12:59.807 --> 01:13:03.368
Rivers will run red with blood
and yellow with urine.

01:13:03.477 --> 01:13:06.674
And a dog will be seen eating cat food
in the land.

01:13:06.781 --> 01:13:10.877
Oh, great king,
your army is the last hope of Cornwood.

01:13:10.985 --> 01:13:16.321
Let us join forces before the light of good
is extinguished forever.

01:13:17.558 --> 01:13:18.991
You calling me crazy?

01:13:19.093 --> 01:13:21.891
Just 'cause I've got a hotel in my foot
don't make me a...

01:13:23.364 --> 01:13:26.026
- Pardon?
- Stop laughing at me, fried avocado.

01:13:32.840 --> 01:13:36.799
Moving along then,
as the only nobleman present who's not...

01:13:38.012 --> 01:13:41.914
I hereby place myself
in command of the royal army.

01:13:42.016 --> 01:13:44.985
- What royal army would that be?
- What?

01:13:45.086 --> 01:13:47.520
King went insane
and declared war on the scallops.

01:13:47.621 --> 01:13:50.249
Tied his army to a boulder
and pushed them into the sea.

01:13:50.357 --> 01:13:51.790
They never returned.

01:13:51.892 --> 01:13:53.655
Scallops must've got them.

01:13:53.761 --> 01:13:56.855
Oh, well. There'll be no epic battle today.

01:14:00.835 --> 01:14:02.803
Methinks we be boned.

01:14:08.776 --> 01:14:09.800
Where's their army?

01:14:09.910 --> 01:14:12.606
Maybe they didn't hear the horn.
Blow it again.

01:14:17.218 --> 01:14:19.652
Man, I'll show that cat how to blow.

01:14:33.100 --> 01:14:38.504
All right. On three. One, two, three.

01:14:40.541 --> 01:14:42.839
Oil in the murder hole.

01:14:45.279 --> 01:14:48.339
What are they pouring
through the murder hole? Hot oil?

01:14:48.449 --> 01:14:50.542
Yeah, I think it might be hot oil.

01:14:52.520 --> 01:14:55.717
I knew it. I was right, Walt. It's hot oil.

01:15:13.240 --> 01:15:14.434
Ow!

01:15:16.877 --> 01:15:19.778
What the... You're not made of Tuesday.

01:15:20.281 --> 01:15:22.181
My sanity. It's back.

01:15:22.283 --> 01:15:25.013
At last, I can live the life I always...

01:16:06.927 --> 01:16:08.087
Ahhh!

01:16:13.300 --> 01:16:16.292
You're going onto sainthood.
Just call the chef.

01:16:26.714 --> 01:16:29.239
- What does it mean?
- It is as we feared.

01:16:29.350 --> 01:16:33.411
- Evil will soon triumph over good.
- Your friends face certain death.

01:16:33.520 --> 01:16:35.681
Followed by a disrespectful
marionette show

01:16:35.789 --> 01:16:37.120
performed with their corpses.

01:16:37.224 --> 01:16:41.558
- No! We've got to do something.
- Believe me, we will.

01:16:41.662 --> 01:16:46.292
We've taken out a sternly worded ad
in tomorrow's Cornwood Times.

01:16:48.736 --> 01:16:50.567
What a load of man-horse manure.

01:16:50.671 --> 01:16:55.870
Well, Legola, if you have a better idea,
perhaps you'd like to challenge me to

01:16:55.976 --> 01:16:57.204
debate.

01:17:13.460 --> 01:17:15.724
I'm too exhausted. I can't go on.

01:17:15.829 --> 01:17:18.593
I'm here for you, my friend.
I'll drag you onward.

01:17:18.699 --> 01:17:22.191
Even to my last ounce of strength.
Grab onto my testicles.

01:17:23.337 --> 01:17:26.602
You know,
I think maybe I can walk after all.

01:17:30.711 --> 01:17:32.440
That's not Wipe Castle.

01:17:32.546 --> 01:17:35.379
The dodeca-call is coming
from inside the house.

01:17:40.287 --> 01:17:44.189
What are you waiting for, Frydo?
Throw it already in the boiling plastic.

01:17:44.291 --> 01:17:47.283
- I would. But...
- Me's enjoys owning it.

01:17:47.394 --> 01:17:49.919
Stop talking like that. It gives me anxiety.

01:17:51.231 --> 01:17:52.493
Ow!

01:17:54.301 --> 01:17:56.360
No!

01:18:02.509 --> 01:18:03.601
Twelve.

01:18:12.786 --> 01:18:17.348
So, it's all come down to this.
A dungeon and dragons.

01:18:17.458 --> 01:18:19.016
I didn't see it coming.

01:18:20.394 --> 01:18:21.486
Wait.

01:18:30.738 --> 01:18:32.865
Eat the wizard,
eat the slut

01:18:32.973 --> 01:18:35.168
Eat the robot's shiny butt

01:18:35.809 --> 01:18:38.903
Well, at least
we'll be remembered in song.

01:18:39.012 --> 01:18:41.742
Wait a second. I have an idea.

01:18:41.849 --> 01:18:44.340
I surrender. Here, eat my friends.

01:18:44.451 --> 01:18:47.648
Just give me one more second
of sweet, sweet life.

01:18:53.460 --> 01:18:56.554
Well, that worked out
pretty good, eh, fellows?

01:18:59.767 --> 01:19:02.531
Prepare to fire again, brave cowards.

01:19:03.904 --> 01:19:05.804
I still say, I won the debate.

01:19:06.607 --> 01:19:07.767
Fire.

01:19:11.478 --> 01:19:12.445
Uh-oh.

01:19:16.550 --> 01:19:17.642
Whew!

01:19:18.852 --> 01:19:21.320
Legola, you saved us.

01:19:21.922 --> 01:19:23.947
How can I ever repay you?

01:19:31.498 --> 01:19:35.662
Frydo is fighting for his life.
The fate of Cornwood is in our hands.

01:19:35.769 --> 01:19:37.737
Quickly, to the Geysers.

01:19:38.605 --> 01:19:42.439
- Can it wait a couple of minutes?
- Yes. Yes, it can.

01:19:57.925 --> 01:20:00.519
You are no match for my dragon style.

01:20:03.831 --> 01:20:06.163
I guess you are
a match for my dragon style.

01:20:06.266 --> 01:20:07.255
Tell me, Frydo,

01:20:07.367 --> 01:20:11.565
are you aware that a dragon's
one weakness is its soft underbelly?

01:20:11.672 --> 01:20:13.139
No. Why do you...

01:20:15.742 --> 01:20:18.074
Get my friend out of your mouth.

01:20:19.146 --> 01:20:20.943
It is all over, Momon.

01:20:21.048 --> 01:20:23.039
We'll soon be down there defeating you.

01:20:23.150 --> 01:20:27.246
And it's all thanks to
the existence of this fragile staircase.

01:20:29.957 --> 01:20:30.924
Whoa!

01:20:37.397 --> 01:20:39.524
Quick. Get on the magic bug.

01:20:39.633 --> 01:20:43.501
It's not a magic bug, you dope.
It's a magic arachnid.

01:20:43.604 --> 01:20:45.868
Can't you count the legs?

01:20:45.973 --> 01:20:50.239
- No.
- Six, seven, eight. Not six, eight.

01:20:50.344 --> 01:20:52.244
I'll kill you, you imbecile.

01:21:04.691 --> 01:21:07.421
My underbelly. My one weakness.

01:21:15.702 --> 01:21:20.469
I got it. Now I can throw it in
the hot thing over there and be the hero.

01:21:20.574 --> 01:21:24.476
On the other hand,
infinite power might be nice.

01:21:27.281 --> 01:21:29.749
Please, I'm trying to help you.

01:21:29.850 --> 01:21:32.011
Then why are you hitting me with a stick?

01:21:32.119 --> 01:21:34.713
How stupid are you
that you think that's helping?

01:21:34.821 --> 01:21:37.722
Mommy never told you about my father.

01:21:37.824 --> 01:21:41.851
- She said he was a foul He-demon.
- Exactly.

01:21:41.962 --> 01:21:44.624
You are my father.

01:21:46.133 --> 01:21:49.330
No. No, that's impossible.

01:21:49.436 --> 01:21:52.405
Search your feelings.
You know it to be true.

01:21:52.506 --> 01:21:55.236
No, no!

01:21:55.342 --> 01:21:57.902
Yeah. I heard Mommy say so.

01:22:03.216 --> 01:22:07.448
I have all the dice.
I am the dungeon master.

01:22:07.554 --> 01:22:09.488
I know all and see...

01:22:13.226 --> 01:22:14.818
Game over.

01:22:33.814 --> 01:22:35.042
No! No!

01:22:48.328 --> 01:22:49.556
What happened?

01:22:52.232 --> 01:22:54.632
My God,
we're out of that weird, crazy world

01:22:54.735 --> 01:22:56.896
and back in our regular crazy world.

01:22:57.537 --> 01:22:59.903
Did we all just
have some kind of freaky dream

01:23:00.007 --> 01:23:01.133
or was it ghosts?

01:23:01.241 --> 01:23:03.869
Neither, Fry. It was science.

01:23:03.977 --> 01:23:08.573
Bender's mighty imagination
amplified by a dark matter resonance

01:23:08.682 --> 01:23:12.880
created an alternate reality
that very nearly blew our minds.

01:23:12.986 --> 01:23:15.352
Exactly.
You can't make that kind of stuff up.

01:23:15.455 --> 01:23:17.355
Quit trying to explain everything.

01:23:17.457 --> 01:23:21.086
I defeated you in that world
and I'll defeat you in this one.

01:23:21.194 --> 01:23:24.493
Boys, the crystal's still in his stomach.

01:23:24.598 --> 01:23:26.122
Commencing intestinal flash flood.

01:23:27.134 --> 01:23:31.628
Wait! Before my moment of shame, can I...

01:23:32.839 --> 01:23:34.329
Yes, speak up.

01:23:38.745 --> 01:23:41.441
Can I give my boy a hug?

01:23:41.982 --> 01:23:46.180
All right. Fine. I've never done it.
I guess somebody should.

01:23:47.154 --> 01:23:48.314
Daddy.

01:23:49.923 --> 01:23:53.120
Like father, like son, eh, boy?

01:23:55.028 --> 01:23:56.859
We both eated the crysals.

01:23:59.266 --> 01:24:01.131
No. No!

01:24:08.775 --> 01:24:11.573
My dark matter. It's worthless.

01:24:11.678 --> 01:24:15.239
That's right, Mom. But fear not, fancy folk.

01:24:15.348 --> 01:24:18.647
For I've just thunk up
an alternative energy source.

01:24:18.752 --> 01:24:22.188
- Nibbler-power.
- Hurray. Wait. What?

01:24:27.728 --> 01:24:29.696
Mush! Mush!

01:24:29.796 --> 01:24:31.730
Whip harder, Professor.

01:24:35.302 --> 01:24:39.466
Faster, faster. Slower.

01:24:46.880 --> 01:24:48.677
One, two
One, two, three

01:25:12.472 --> 01:25:13.996
All rise
Attention

01:25:45.205 --> 01:25:46.968
All rise
Attention

01:25:53.380 --> 01:25:54.813
All rise
Attention

01:26:02.823 --> 01:26:04.381
Twenty-four
I'm gonna get twenty four

01:26:04.491 --> 01:26:06.482
I'm gonna get 24th century
on his ass

01:26:45.565 --> 01:26:46.532
Anyone wanna play

01:26:46.633 --> 01:26:49.007
Dungeons &amp; Dragons for
the next quadrillion years?
